History-Search: No public issue, pull request, commit message, or review comment
 documents a choice to discard ChromosomeAccession. Commit
 4ea4433c09755f55b952d8f7fcb2093bae0dedbb introduced the Chromosome-field
 projection; pull request 3 later added a standard-chromosome filter for
 ChrUn, and pull request 4 addressed X/Y key collisions.
Conclusion: The official ClinVar VCF retains alternate sequence accessions for
 all 40 rows. RClinVarbitration follows the official VCF. The pinned upstream
 seven-column oracle remains intentionally available for bug-for-bug policy
 conformance, but its primary-looking CHROM values are not coordinate-safe.
